From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:57:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 091/202] [ae-patch] Show the rail's context and connectors as
 loading while Claude starts, and keep "Try again" for a lost connection

A new session's first context probe reached the runner before Claude had started: no statusLine reading, no session id or no live process yet. Each of those came back as the same error as a real failure, started a 30-second backoff, and the web cached the error as a good answer for three minutes, so the rail's Context and Connectors sections showed "Could not read Claude context" until a manual refresh.

The runner now raises ContextNotReady for those three cases and answers pending without recording a failure, and it logs real failures (class and a path-trimmed first line). The server marks a runner-offline or timed-out answer offline. The web store never treats an unavailable answer as fresh, retries pending and other not-offline answers quietly (2, 4, 8, 16, then 30 seconds, for about two minutes) before letting the reason and Try again show, shows an offline answer at once, and reloads when the focused session's turn ends.
